    {
      "id": "decl-meaning",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Meaning",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": -1400,
        "y": -400
      },
      "width": 480,
      "height": 320,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "ac97492b-7402-428b-9bce-5c5e91c7f981"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Meaning\n\n**What is this thing?**\n\nDeclaration is the artifact-level contract that gives a graph durable identity, intent, authority, dependencies, and exposed surfaces. It is a graph's semantic anchor and its implicit root — the entry point every consumer reaches first, without inventing a separate root node merely for plumbing.\n\nA graph without a Declaration is a fragment: content that hasn't yet been given an identity of its own."
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "decl-invariants",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Invariants",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": -860,
        "y": -400
      },
      "width": 480,
      "height": 320,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "ac97492b-7402-428b-9bce-5c5e91c7f981"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Invariants\n\n**What makes this thing a Declaration, specifically?**\n\n- Exactly one authoritative Declaration per graph (a fragment may have none; it never has two).\n- Owns `data.identity` — `graphId`, `name`, `version`, `description` — for the graph as a whole.\n- Owns `data.intent` — `kind` and `scope` — stating what kind of artifact this graph is.\n- Is reachable as the graph's implicit root port even when no other node explicitly claims that role.\n- Every other node that belongs to this graph shares its `graphId`."
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "decl-contract",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Contract",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": -320,
        "y": -400
      },
      "width": 480,
      "height": 320,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "ac97492b-7402-428b-9bce-5c5e91c7f981"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Contract\n\n**What data belongs to it?**\n\n```text\nidentity      { graphId, name, version, description }\nintent        { kind, scope }\ndeclaration   { kind, targetMode, defaultSurfaceId, surfaces[] }\ndependencies  { nodeTypes[], portContracts[], schemaVersions }\nauthority     { mutation{allowCreate,allowUpdate,allowDelete}, actors{humans,agents,tools} }\nsettings      { layout, autoSave, github{path} }\ndocument      { url }\n```\n\nRequired at minimum: `identity.graphId`, `identity.name`, `identity.version`, `identity.description`, `intent.kind`, `intent.scope`, `declaration.kind`."
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "decl-ports",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Ports and Relationships",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": 220,
        "y": -400
      },
      "width": 480,
      "height": 320,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "ac97492b-7402-428b-9bce-5c5e91c7f981"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Ports and Relationships\n\n**What semantic relationships does it expose?**\n\n- `default-view` — the graph's primary detail-level representation.\n- `summary-view`, `icon-view`, `glyph` — shared collapsed representations, each optional.\n- `landing-surface` — what a portal lands on when entering this graph.\n- `port` (repeatable) — an exposed, named entry point other than the defaults above.\n\nEach relationship **assigns** another node to a named role. The role lives on the Declaration's edge to that node, not as a property intrinsic to the node itself — the same node could be assigned a different role, or none, without changing anything about the node."
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "decl-behavior",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Behavior",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": 760,
        "y": -400
      },
      "width": 480,
      "height": 320,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "ac97492b-7402-428b-9bce-5c5e91c7f981"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Behavior\n\n**What does it participate in?**\n\nDeclaration does not itself run in the property/event/method runtime — that's node-level behavior elsewhere in the graph. What Declaration does is gate what's *allowed* to exist: `dependencies.nodeTypes` names which node types this graph may contain, and `authority.mutation` states whether creation, update, and deletion are permitted at all, for this graph, by humans, agents, and tools respectively."
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "decl-representations",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Representations",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": 1300,
        "y": -400
      },
      "width": 480,
      "height": 320,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "ac97492b-7402-428b-9bce-5c5e91c7f981"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Representations\n\n**How is it represented?**\n\nA Declaration typically renders as a compact identity card at detail level — name, description, version — not the graph's full content. Collapsed, it shows the graph's own declared glyph if one exists, or a generic declaration mark otherwise. Declaration never renders the content assigned to its own default-view/summary-view/icon-view relationships as if it were that content — it renders itself, and *points at* those relationships."
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "decl-boundary",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Explicitly Not Part of This Primitive",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": -1400,
        "y": 260
      },
      "width": 480,
      "height": 340,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "ac97492b-7402-428b-9bce-5c5e91c7f981"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Explicitly Not Part of This Primitive\n\n- Declaration does not render content. Rendering the graph's actual material is View and Content's job; Declaration only names which node fills each presentation role.\n- Declaration does not own node positions or layout. Where nodes sit on the canvas is unrelated to identity.\n- Declaration does not define *how* an exposed view looks — only *which* node is assigned to that role.\n- Declaration does not grant runtime capability beyond what `authority` explicitly states. Absence of a grant means the action is not permitted, not that it's merely undocumented.\n- Declaration is not a template. It describes one graph's own identity, not a reusable composition pattern for building other graphs (see Templates)."
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "decl-examples",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Examples",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": -860,
        "y": 260
      },
      "width": 480,
      "height": 340,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "ac97492b-7402-428b-9bce-5c5e91c7f981"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Examples\n\n**Examples live outside the primitive, referenced, not embedded.**\n\nNo example graphs are linked yet — this primitive was authored before any instance graph was built specifically to demonstrate it. Add a portal here to a real graph's Declaration once one exists specifically as a worked example, rather than folding a demo into this spec.\n\nEvery primitive graph this session built tonight (`qa/workspace-persistence.node`, `ideas/n8n-style-automation-template/root.node`, `topics/twilite-automation-readiness/root.node`) already has a real Declaration node and could each serve as a citable example — not yet linked here as a deliberate choice, since this primitive spec should name examples on purpose, not by convenience."
        }
      }
    }
  ],
